From afc2332de2afbc3361a4bca1c1e0617f1202637f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 04:39:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 870/871] dspark: cache constant mask-token embedding for query
 blocks

DSpark query blocks place the anchor token at offset 0 and repeat the
constant parallel_drafting_token_id across offsets 1..block_size-1 for
every request. Feeding the entire [num_reqs * block_size] block through
VocabParallelEmbedding performs a block_size-times larger lookup and TP
all-reduce on every decode step.

Precompute and cache the constant mask-token embedding once after draft
weight loading (cache_mask_embed) and embed only the num_reqs anchor
tokens per step (embed_query_block), broadcasting the cached vector into
the mask positions. This is bit-exact against full block embedding and
shrinks the draft embedding lookup and TP collective by 5x on DeepSeek
V4.1 Flash (6x when sample_from_anchor is False).

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 + candidate-74 (0001..0869)
Quality impact: none (bit-exact embeddings)
Tests: tests/v1/spec_decode/test_dspark_mask_embed_cache.py
Upstream status: local candidate-76 patch
